From 9f768771cfb9dc07cec2ec0b9d866d99d735f49b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 01:30:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] updates: no LibreELEC update server, manual updates and HTTPS
 only

Hades is LibreELEC plus Dolby Vision: an official LibreELEC build offered by
the LibreELEC update server would replace it and drop Dolby Vision, and the
init now refuses it anyway. Until a Hades update channel exists:

- the update server URLs are empty, so nothing is requested on start-up or
  every 6 hours (before, the check ran even with automatic updates off and
  sent the machine-id by default);
- "available versions" explains how to update from a local .tar file;
- custom channels keep working.

Defaults change to manual updates and no statistics; both remain options.
Update data and images are only fetched over HTTPS (http:// is upgraded,
other schemes except file:// are refused): images used to be downloaded
over plain HTTP, and they carry no signature, only md5 files inside the
same archive. An unreachable official channel no longer breaks the custom
channels (None was indexed as a dict).
